## Proposed Technical Changes

### 1. Data Contracts & Type Definitions
#### [NEW] [clientBilling.ts](file:///d:/Joy%20PeopleHR%20new%20version/workforceos-enterprise-hrms/src/types/clientBilling.ts)
Comprehensive TypeScript interfaces for:
- `ClientMaster`: Legal name, code, GSTIN, PAN, state code, addresses, payment terms.
- `ClientContract`: Contract number, service type (Manpower, Security, Facility, etc.), SAC code (default 998519), billing cycle, validity dates.
- `EmployeeClientDeployment`: Effective-dated mapping of employee to client, contract, site location, department, shift, and wage structure.
- `SalaryDivisorType`: `CALENDAR_DAYS`, `FIXED_26`, `FIXED_30`, `FIXED_31`, `WORKING_DAYS`, `CLIENT_CUSTOM`.
- `BillingRule`: Calculation methods (`FIXED_AMOUNT`, `PERCENTAGE_OF_GROSS`, `PERCENTAGE_OF_BASIC`, `PERCENTAGE_OF_BILLABLE_WAGES`, `PER_EMPLOYEE`, `PER_DAY`, `PER_HOUR`, `PER_OT_HOUR`, `CUSTOM_FORMULA`), priority, charge category, effective date ranges.
- `BillingConfiguration`: Toggleable billable salary components, employer contribution pass-through flags, recovery deduction treatments.
- `BillingRun`: Full lifecycle state (`DRAFT` $\rightarrow$ `CALCULATED` $\rightarrow$ `AUDIT_REVIEW` $\rightarrow$ `FINANCE_REVIEW` $\rightarrow$ `APPROVED` $\rightarrow$ `INVOICE_GENERATED` $\rightarrow$ `PAID` $\rightarrow$ `CLOSED`).
- `BillingEmployeeResult`: Attendance breakdown, earnings, deductions, employer EPF/EPS/EDLI/ESI/LWF, billable component breakdown.
- `BillingStatutoryReconciliation`: Payroll vs. Billing comparison for employee counts, pay days, OT hours, employer PF, and employer ESI.
- `BillingInvoice`: Generated tax invoice with SAC code, CGST/SGST/IGST breakup, amount in words (Indian numbering format), and immutable calculation snapshots.
- `ExcelTemplateMapping`: Configurable mapping configuration connecting SaaS fields to client legacy templates.

